---
title: Tuna with Soy Sauce, Ginger and Chilli
description: Seared tuna steaks in a rich balsamic glaze
author: Rick Stein
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en_GB
prep time: 15m
cook time: 2m
difficulty: Medium
tags:
- seafood
- main-course
- savoury
---

Bring a pan of salted water to the boil. Drop in the @egg noodles{250%g}, cover and take off the heat. Leave to soak for ~{4%minutes}.

Meanwhile, heat a #frying pan{} over a high heat until quite hot. Add the @sunflower oil{1%tbsp} and @thick tuna loin steaks{4}(175 g each) and sear over a high heat for ~{30%seconds} on each side.

Take the pan off the heat and add the @dark soy sauce{6%tbsp} and @balsamic vinegar{4%tbsp}. Simmer on low heat for ~{2%minutes}. Turn the steaks over (be careful not to splash yourself), sprinkle with the @garlic{1%large clove}(finely chopped), @root ginger{1%inch}(finely diced) and @bird eye chilli{1}(finely chopped) and simmer for a further ~{1%minute}.

Place the tuna on four warmed plates, spoon over the sauce, and pile the @spring onions{3}(cut into 2 inch pieces and finely shredded lengthways) on top of each steak. Drain the noodles, tip them into a serving bowl and toss with the @sesame oil{1%tsp}. Serve with the tuna.